then they're pretty much done.

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:51.000
But that's not true at all

00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:55.000
You have to complete original research

00:42:55.000 --> 00:43:02.000
And a written research dissertation to be graduated

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:07.000
And the PhD, the milestones are the candidacy exam

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:13.000
That you should take near the completion of your 18-hour core

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:17.000
And find a dissertation advisor

00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:21.000
It's an oral exam with three other

00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:25.000
information science or computer science faculty members

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:32.000
complete the online ethics training for research ethics

00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:41.000
Select your dissertation committee. Now it's four members, advisor and three other faculty. And one of those others can be an external

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:45.000
Somebody from industry or another university

00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:53.000
Then the most critical point in the PhD program is defending your research proposal

00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:57.000
The research proposal is basically your statement of work

00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:03.000
Once you say this is the research I'm going to do and here's how I'm going to do it

00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:07.000
And your advisor and your three other faculty on your committee approve it

00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:19.000
Then now, all you need to do is finish what you said you were going to do, and you will complete your degree. So think of it as a statement of work, and it should be done as early as you can

00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:28.000
Because what holds up most people from completing their PhD is their research.

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:32.000
Unfortunately, I've had some students that's

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:35.000
Actually, 10 years

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:43.000
It wasn't because they were working on a really, really hard proposal. It's just because they

00:44:43.000 --> 00:44:52.000
Could not gather the time and energy and the focus that it takes to complete their research in a reasonable amount of time.

00:44:52.000 --> 00:45:03.000
So, starting your research early, getting on a good track, being sure it's something where you can get data, that is doable, you can see it all the way through to the end is key.

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:09.000
And so the final was to complete research and write a dissertation

00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:14.000
We do have a couple of other new

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:26.000
requirements. One of them now is completing a research paper. Most people do that anyway, but we wanted to make it a requirement to be sure that everyone does publish research

00:45:26.000 --> 00:45:28.000
During their PhD

00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:33.000
So these are some others that we put in paper publication

00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:43.000
Also, this minimum time is the opposite. Some people, instead of not starting their proposal early

00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:59.000
Wait until they finish their research to make a proposal. I guess they're afraid that their research might not be good. So they want to wait and see how it turns out before they propose it, which is exactly the opposite of what should be done

00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:04.000
So we've had to impose, at least to keep things sane

00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:12.000
an interval, a forced interval between the proposal and defense of your dissertation, which is now at least 7 months

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:29.000
So that would mean that somebody that's planning to graduate in May of next year would need to defend their proposal if they haven't already done so. Most of the people would have already done so, but at a minimum would have to defend it in September

00:46:29.000 --> 00:46:33.000
To meet the minimum requirement

00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:41.000
Another thing is, and again, this mostly applies to people that are struggling to kind of finish their research

00:46:41.000 --> 00:46:44.000
is you have to continue to stay enrolled

00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:48.000
Even if you've achieved your 42 hours

00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:56.000
You still have to keep taking… you have to be enrolled every spring and fall in order to maintain your status in the program.

00:46:56.000 --> 00:47:01.000
And the reason for that is that you're still going to be using university resources, you're going to be

00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:09.000
working with your advisor and your committee while you're working on your research, so you have to stay enrolled, but at least

00:47:09.000 --> 00:47:14.000
But it only requires being enrolled at least one hour

00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:19.000
So, you have to remember to do that, otherwise you'll get dropped from the program

00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:23.000
And so I have to start over again, so you don't want to do that.

00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:34.000
So you need to stay consecutively or continuously enrolled in the program until you defend your final dissertation.

